  --- the MINT GATE, rebuilt so it cannot miss by ENCODING (RULING CG) ---
  A probe ASKS 'is G59 absent?' and answers 'yes' whenever it cannot read the
  token.  This instead ENUMERATES the whole address population and asserts it is
  CONTIGUOUS: an address written in an encoding the scanner misses would open a
  HOLE, and a hole is VISIBLE.  Absence is then a consequence of completeness,
  not a probe's silence.  This is the uniqueness claim RULING CG asked for.
